WEBVTT

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:02.850
<b>Inter-High Road Race</b>

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:06.680
Hakone Academy!

00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:07.610
Go!

00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:10.530
Go, Sohoku!

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:12.530
Kyoto Fushimi!

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:16.450
Huh?

00:00:16.790 --> 00:00:18.990
Kaburagi, how are you feeling?

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:20.160
Huh? What was that?

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:26.310
I can't hear anything over the crowd!

00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:28.460
You seem pretty nervous.

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:29.750
Nervous?

00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:31.590
About the Inter-High?

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:33.280
As if!

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:34.800
Your anger's misplaced...

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:38.730
I-Is Kaburagi-kun okay?

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:40.570
He collapsed yesterday.

00:00:40.570 --> 00:00:45.060
He's experienced firsthand that the 
Inter-High is bigger than he thought.

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:49.510
I'm pathetic.

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:53.080
I can't believe I collapsed.

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:54.030
Damn it.

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:57.010
I thought you didn't need to worry.

00:00:57.010 --> 00:00:59.080
Isn't God on your side?

00:00:59.390 --> 00:01:01.040
Yeah, but...

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:02.830
<i>He's not denying it.</i>

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:04.160
Kaburagi...

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:06.170
Huh? What was that, Aoyagi?

00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:08.670
Hey, watch your mouth.

00:01:09.570 --> 00:01:11.090
These are for you.

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:13.640
G-God's stationery?

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:14.810
Why do you have those?

00:01:14.810 --> 00:01:16.010
So many of them, too!

00:01:16.010 --> 00:01:17.180
Please...

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:17.790
Aoyagi.

00:01:17.790 --> 00:01:18.420
Give those...

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:18.970
...to me!

00:01:19.480 --> 00:01:21.890
What's your problem? Aren't they for me?

00:01:21.890 --> 00:01:23.980
I was told to give them to 
you at the appropriate time.

00:01:23.980 --> 00:01:25.660
What does "appropriate" mean?

00:01:25.660 --> 00:01:26.890
<i>He's an idiot.</i>

00:01:26.890 --> 00:01:30.150
It means under the right circumstances.

00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:32.320
First, calm yourself.

00:01:39.860 --> 00:01:41.740
Got it!

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:45.290
<i>Aoyagi-san tamed Kaburagi!</i>

00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:47.370
I've regained my composure.

00:01:47.970 --> 00:01:49.080
Good.

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:50.840
Now, give me the notes.

00:01:51.350 --> 00:01:53.050
I'll give them to you if you follow me.

00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:54.130
You cheapskate, Aoyagi!

00:01:54.490 --> 00:01:55.910
You mean, "Aoyagi-san."

00:01:55.910 --> 00:01:57.760
Sorry.

00:01:58.450 --> 00:02:00.010
Follow me. Don't fall behind.

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:01.340
Piece of cake.

00:02:01.340 --> 00:02:03.010
<i>The race will begin shortly.</i>

00:02:04.990 --> 00:02:08.020
<i>I'm nervous. My hands are shaking.</i>

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:12.020
<i>But the start of the race won't wait.</i>

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:16.030
<i>I must calm myself and steel my resolve.</i>

00:02:16.460 --> 00:02:19.990
<i>The second day of the Inter-High is starting.</i>

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:29.670
<b><i>Yowamushi Pedal</i></b>

00:02:29.830 --> 00:02:31.750
<b><i>Yowamushi Pedal</i></b>

00:03:53.870 --> 00:03:58.340
<i>LINE.08  Second Day, Start!!</i>

00:03:54.020 --> 00:03:58.380
<i>The second day and stage of 
the Inter-High has begun!</i>

00:03:59.490 --> 00:04:00.630
Let's go! It's the second day!

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:03.010
We won't lose today!

00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:06.180
You're here, hotshot?

00:04:06.670 --> 00:04:08.390
I'm here, Naruko.

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:16.370
The Inter-High follows special rules.

00:04:16.370 --> 00:04:17.690
We start in the order we finished.

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:22.190
Yesterday we finished three minutes 
and 15 seconds after first.

00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:26.330
Today we start three minutes 
and 15 seconds behind.

00:04:26.330 --> 00:04:27.020
Yes, sir.

00:04:27.020 --> 00:04:28.410
Why are you stopping me?

00:04:29.070 --> 00:04:31.140
They already left!

00:04:31.140 --> 00:04:33.300
Let's go! Aoyagi, come on!

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:36.790
How many times did I tell you we 
start in the order we finished?

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:37.970
What?

00:04:38.530 --> 00:04:39.780
Kaburagi-kun...

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:40.920
Onoda...

00:04:41.430 --> 00:04:46.140
Before we start, I should thank you 
for rescuing me in the mountains.

00:04:46.530 --> 00:04:48.750
Thanks to you, I'm here to see this sight.

00:04:48.750 --> 00:04:50.640
Starting in ten seconds.

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:53.570
Just seeing this makes my hair stand on end.

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:56.100
Nine, eight, seven, six...

00:04:53.570 --> 00:04:56.650
This view from the second 
day's starting line.

00:04:56.650 --> 00:05:03.070
Five, four, three, two, one!

00:05:00.510 --> 00:05:03.070
Cycling really is the best.

00:05:04.630 --> 00:05:05.450
Yes, sir!

00:05:11.670 --> 00:05:12.120
Huh?

00:05:12.580 --> 00:05:14.910
You're back, Teshima-san.

00:05:15.240 --> 00:05:16.540
Hey, Manami.

00:05:16.940 --> 00:05:18.290
You were exhausted.

00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:20.020
And who did that to me?

00:05:21.190 --> 00:05:24.150
I recovered as only an ordinary man can.

00:05:24.150 --> 00:05:26.760
Recovery is key in multi-stage races.

00:05:27.140 --> 00:05:29.430
I'm excited to see how you do.

00:05:30.190 --> 00:05:31.910
<i>Manami-kun seems happy.</i>

00:05:32.450 --> 00:05:37.440
<i>Yesterday they fought, gave everything
 they had, and came to understand each other.</i>

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:40.940
<i>Yesterday morning, they'd never
 even spoken before.</i>

00:05:41.450 --> 00:05:43.220
<i>Bicycles brought them together.</i>

00:05:43.750 --> 00:05:47.700
<i>Manami-kun is happy Teshima-san 
has returned to the race.</i>

00:05:48.050 --> 00:05:50.570
<i>Bicycles really are amazing!</i>

00:05:51.130 --> 00:05:52.200
<i>Let's go.</i>

00:05:52.710 --> 00:05:55.130
<i>I don't know what will happen next,</i>

00:05:55.700 --> 00:05:58.870
<i>but I'll follow this road to 
the second day's finish line...</i>

00:05:58.870 --> 00:06:01.100
<i>By the strength of all six of us!</i>

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:04.770
The race has started!

00:06:04.770 --> 00:06:06.980
Does everyone remember their orders?

00:06:06.980 --> 00:06:07.590
Yes, sir!

00:06:08.650 --> 00:06:10.550
Let's go over the second day's course.

00:06:10.960 --> 00:06:13.220
The race starts at yesterday's finish line.

00:06:13.220 --> 00:06:16.910
We'll ride north on National Route 120,

00:06:16.910 --> 00:06:19.310
which cuts through Senjougahara 
at 1,400 meters above sea level.

00:06:19.670 --> 00:06:23.310
The long, winding climb begins shortly 
after the starting line,

00:06:23.310 --> 00:06:25.190
and rises to approximately 1,800 meters.

00:06:25.650 --> 00:06:29.320
The road leads to the Konsei Pass
 and the Konsei Tunnel.

00:06:29.810 --> 00:06:33.450
After clearing the pass, 
we'll enter a long downhill.

00:06:34.050 --> 00:06:38.160
Past the ski slope and lake is 
a downhill-sloping flat road.

00:06:38.570 --> 00:06:40.920
We'll pass by the scenic Fukiware Falls,

00:06:41.350 --> 00:06:45.860
through Numata City where
 Route 120 ends, then keep on riding.

00:06:46.390 --> 00:06:49.720
It's the longest stage of the three-day race.

00:06:50.380 --> 00:06:52.710
Imaizumi, meet up with Naruko immediately.

00:06:52.710 --> 00:06:53.390
Yes, sir.

00:06:53.780 --> 00:06:56.260
The rest of us will follow.

00:06:56.260 --> 00:06:58.530
The mountains begin shortly after we start.

00:06:58.530 --> 00:06:59.270
Onoda...

00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:03.810
Climb as hard as you can and 
catch up to Imaizumi and Naruko!

00:07:03.810 --> 00:07:04.550
Yes, sir!

00:07:05.540 --> 00:07:07.650
Those are practically the 
same orders I got last year.

00:07:10.590 --> 00:07:13.790
To be honest, Sohoku is barely hanging on.

00:07:13.790 --> 00:07:19.000
But we have two advantages 
going into the second day.

00:07:19.990 --> 00:07:21.290
It's the leading pack!

00:07:21.290 --> 00:07:23.500
Two Sohoku riders are in front!

00:07:24.010 --> 00:07:26.840
First, we have two guys in the front.

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:30.270
Imaizumi and Naruko had nearly 
the same times yesterday.

00:07:30.270 --> 00:07:31.680
They'll be able to meet up immediately.

00:07:32.500 --> 00:07:35.510
Together, they'll be able to 
keep the other teams in check.

00:07:36.140 --> 00:07:39.850
And if they use a rotation,
 they can conserve their strength.

00:07:39.850 --> 00:07:44.190
In other words, we can move 
the front at our own pace.

00:07:44.190 --> 00:07:46.570
Now this makes it easy to ride.

00:07:46.570 --> 00:07:49.400
Try to catch up quickly, Teshima-san!

00:07:49.990 --> 00:07:51.740
The other advantage is...

00:07:53.860 --> 00:07:55.610
We've entered the mountains!

00:07:55.610 --> 00:07:56.410
I'm moving up!

00:07:56.740 --> 00:07:58.580
We're counting on you, Onoda!

00:07:59.200 --> 00:08:02.030
Our other advantage isn't certain.

00:08:02.030 --> 00:08:03.750
It depends on what Hakone Academy does.

00:08:04.220 --> 00:08:07.980
If Hakone Academy slows its pace 
when we enter the mountains,

00:08:07.980 --> 00:08:10.760
move up and pedal as hard as you can.

00:08:10.760 --> 00:08:13.340
It'll be our chance to get 
ahead of Hakone Academy.

00:08:14.680 --> 00:08:16.740
Hakone Academy isn't slowing down.

00:08:16.740 --> 00:08:17.350
Not yet.

00:08:17.720 --> 00:08:22.320
Teshima-san, weren't your 
orders this morning too vague?

00:08:22.320 --> 00:08:24.650
Move up if Hakone Academy slows down?

00:08:24.650 --> 00:08:27.520
Why would they ever do that?

00:08:29.290 --> 00:08:30.820
Hakone Academy is accelerating!

00:08:31.290 --> 00:08:32.540
Don't fall behind, Onoda!

00:08:32.540 --> 00:08:33.150
Yes, sir!

00:08:37.710 --> 00:08:40.480
If we fall behind now, 
having two riders in front

00:08:40.480 --> 00:08:42.750
and our other chances will go up in smoke!

00:08:50.010 --> 00:08:52.260
Hakone Academy is accelerating again!

00:08:52.260 --> 00:08:53.850
Don't let them get away, Onoda!

00:08:53.850 --> 00:08:54.690
Yes, sir!

00:08:57.940 --> 00:09:01.050
Soon. They'll slow down soon.

00:09:01.050 --> 00:09:02.630
That's what I would do.

00:09:03.730 --> 00:09:05.340
We need to make them slow down!

00:09:05.340 --> 00:09:07.980
Try to get ahead of Hakone Academy, 
even if it's just for a second!

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:09.980
Once we make it past that turn...

00:09:11.180 --> 00:09:12.360
Pull as hard as you can!

00:09:12.360 --> 00:09:14.070
Yes, sir!

00:09:25.110 --> 00:09:25.910
They...

00:09:26.330 --> 00:09:27.790
<i>They slowed down!</i>

00:09:29.030 --> 00:09:30.270
You can't be serious!

00:09:30.270 --> 00:09:32.950
What's going on? Are they already exhausted?

00:09:32.950 --> 00:09:33.460
No!

00:09:33.790 --> 00:09:34.860
Go, Onoda!

00:09:34.860 --> 00:09:36.300
Now's our chance to get ahead!

00:09:36.610 --> 00:09:37.420
Yes, sir!

00:09:37.900 --> 00:09:39.300
They actually slowed down.

00:09:39.680 --> 00:09:41.220
It's what I would do.

00:09:41.710 --> 00:09:45.520
Hakone Academy has one more, 
Kuroda, left on their team!

00:09:45.890 --> 00:09:50.570
Kuroda didn't move for a while after 
he fell before the finish line.

00:09:50.570 --> 00:09:54.030
He finished after we did.

00:09:54.860 --> 00:09:56.780
Kuroda is part of Hakone 
Academy's chain of command.

00:09:57.100 --> 00:09:59.450
They'll want him to ride with them.

00:09:59.990 --> 00:10:01.030
Wow...

00:10:01.440 --> 00:10:03.570
That's how I knew they would slow down.

00:10:03.570 --> 00:10:05.940
If we pass Hakone Academy 
and keep up this pace,

00:10:05.940 --> 00:10:08.170
Sohoku will have an overwhelming advantage!

00:10:08.500 --> 00:10:09.900
<i>Amazing.</i>

00:10:09.900 --> 00:10:12.940
<i>The first day's results 
have given us an advantage.</i>

00:10:14.740 --> 00:10:17.810
I thought they were exhausted.

00:10:22.970 --> 00:10:24.190
Whoops!

00:10:24.190 --> 00:10:25.490
I spaced out.

00:10:25.490 --> 00:10:27.940
I could never fall behind here.

00:10:31.980 --> 00:10:35.030
Teshima-san, is this pace okay?

00:10:35.030 --> 00:10:37.380
We'll be able to group up
 with the others soon.

00:10:37.380 --> 00:10:39.770
Yeah. Keep it up, Onoda!

00:10:45.230 --> 00:10:46.450
Huh? What?

00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:53.790
Onoda, let's switch.

00:10:53.790 --> 00:10:54.620
Yes, sir.

00:10:58.540 --> 00:11:01.430
We can stay ahead of them while 
they're picking up Kuroda!

00:11:01.430 --> 00:11:03.820
Let's get our team together before they do!

00:11:03.820 --> 00:11:04.720
Yes, sir!

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:06.270
What's wrong, Kaburagi?

00:11:06.270 --> 00:11:07.620
I can't hear you!

00:11:07.620 --> 00:11:08.310
Are you keeping—

00:11:11.650 --> 00:11:12.900
What is it?

00:11:14.750 --> 00:11:16.190
I answered.

00:11:16.660 --> 00:11:18.290
We're headed for the front, right?

00:11:18.290 --> 00:11:21.570
Let's get ahead of
 Hakone Academy and that pig.

00:11:21.570 --> 00:11:23.940
All right. I like your enthusiasm.

00:11:23.940 --> 00:11:25.620
It'll be hard, but make sure you keep up.

00:11:26.570 --> 00:11:28.140
Who do you think you're talking to?

00:11:28.140 --> 00:11:31.040
I'm the genius all-rounder Kaburagi Issa!

00:11:31.040 --> 00:11:33.040
Sounds promising.

00:11:35.190 --> 00:11:36.630
<i>That was close.</i>

00:11:36.630 --> 00:11:39.510
<i>I couldn't keep up with the pace we're 
keeping to pull ahead of Hakone Academy.</i>

00:11:40.090 --> 00:11:41.750
<i>Someone as great as me...</i>

00:11:43.810 --> 00:11:45.390
<i>Maybe I'm not in top shape.</i>

00:11:46.070 --> 00:11:47.720
<i>I feel out of sync.</i>

00:11:47.720 --> 00:11:48.640
<i>I did earlier, too.</i>

00:11:49.620 --> 00:11:51.140
Huh? What?

00:11:52.090 --> 00:11:53.100
What?

00:11:53.580 --> 00:11:55.290
Why are my feet on the ground?

00:11:55.290 --> 00:11:57.260
I can't get left behind here.

00:11:57.260 --> 00:11:58.360
This isn't good.

00:11:58.850 --> 00:12:02.690
<i>I'm Kaburagi Issa, the man who 
will make Sohoku stronger.</i>

00:12:02.690 --> 00:12:08.780
<i>I'm secretly aiming to stand on the 
highest point of the final winner's podium.</i>

00:12:08.780 --> 00:12:11.790
Damn it!

00:12:14.540 --> 00:12:18.090
<i>It's so tough, I couldn't 
respond to Teshima-san.</i>

00:12:18.570 --> 00:12:20.090
Are you keeping up?

00:12:20.090 --> 00:12:21.920
It seemed like you were falling behind.

00:12:22.230 --> 00:12:24.310
What? You must be seeing things!

00:12:24.310 --> 00:12:25.900
Are you sure you don't need glasses?

00:12:25.900 --> 00:12:26.940
I see.

00:12:29.090 --> 00:12:31.390
<i>I'm glad Aoyagi-san's an idiot.</i>

00:12:31.390 --> 00:12:34.340
<i>I just have to make it 
to the top of the pass.</i>

00:12:34.340 --> 00:12:36.440
<i>Keep at it. You'll be okay.</i>

00:12:37.230 --> 00:12:41.650
<i>They won't be able to group up with 
third-year Kuroda that quickly, anyway.</i>

00:12:44.700 --> 00:12:47.100
Hakone Academy's fallen back to the pack?

00:12:47.100 --> 00:12:47.820
What's going on?

00:12:47.820 --> 00:12:49.830
Is someone not feeling well?

00:12:49.830 --> 00:12:52.000
Doesn't look that way to me.

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:55.850
Are they waiting for #12 so their 
whole team can ride together?

00:12:55.850 --> 00:12:58.840
So they slowed down and 
fell back to the pack?

00:13:00.380 --> 00:13:02.400
Everyone's here now.

00:13:02.400 --> 00:13:03.890
Let's go.

00:13:03.890 --> 00:13:04.760
Abs ready...

00:13:05.070 --> 00:13:06.200
Go!

00:13:06.820 --> 00:13:08.180
Hakone Academy's charging ahead!

00:13:08.180 --> 00:13:08.890
They're fast!

00:13:08.890 --> 00:13:13.390
There's still only five of them, 
but it's like all six of them are there!

00:13:13.390 --> 00:13:15.390
The second day's going to get crazy.

00:13:15.390 --> 00:13:17.730
Sohoku's trying to stay ahead as four!

00:13:17.730 --> 00:13:20.570
Hakone Academy's chasing from behind as five!

00:13:23.740 --> 00:13:26.900
<i>I'm okay now. I've gotten used to the pace.</i>

00:13:26.900 --> 00:13:28.460
<i>I won't fall behind.</i>

00:13:28.910 --> 00:13:31.330
<i>I just have to keep climbing.</i>

00:13:33.580 --> 00:13:36.860
<i>Please slow down a little...</i>

00:13:36.160 --> 00:13:37.870
Are you okay, Kaburagi?

00:13:37.870 --> 00:13:39.170
You look pale.

00:13:39.170 --> 00:13:41.230
What? I'm fine.

00:13:41.230 --> 00:13:42.990
Maybe it's the light.

00:13:42.990 --> 00:13:44.990
Seriously, I'm great.

00:13:45.840 --> 00:13:47.650
Piece of cake.

00:13:48.740 --> 00:13:50.170
<i>I can't say it.</i>

00:13:50.170 --> 00:13:53.010
<i>I can't ask them to lower the pace.</i>

00:13:53.930 --> 00:13:55.580
<i>It would be too lame.</i>

00:13:56.770 --> 00:13:58.680
Sorry, Touichirou.

00:13:58.680 --> 00:14:00.940
We only did what made sense, Yuki.

00:14:01.460 --> 00:14:03.400
We're stronger this way!

00:14:03.400 --> 00:14:05.860
Welcome back, Kuroda-san.

00:14:05.860 --> 00:14:07.950
Thanks, Manami. Have you been good?

00:14:07.950 --> 00:14:09.770
Don't drawl.

00:14:09.770 --> 00:14:12.330
You're not serious enough, Manami.

00:14:12.750 --> 00:14:13.850
<i>It's rising.</i>

00:14:13.850 --> 00:14:16.330
<i>Just having Yuki around 
raises the team's morale.</i>

00:14:17.300 --> 00:14:20.890
<i>Think you've gotten ahead of us, Teshima-kun?</i>

00:14:21.630 --> 00:14:25.500
<i>Did you think you'd have an 
advantage if you caught up first?</i>

00:14:26.090 --> 00:14:28.080
Too bad.

00:14:28.080 --> 00:14:31.220
You're not the ones who will 
catch up to the front first.

00:14:32.580 --> 00:14:34.220
<i>Calm down, Frank.</i>

00:14:34.890 --> 00:14:38.120
<i>It's a long ten-kilometer 
climb to the Konsei Pass.</i>

00:14:38.120 --> 00:14:40.100
<i>How long can you stay ahead?</i>

00:14:40.100 --> 00:14:41.270
<i>Or...</i>

00:14:43.980 --> 00:14:45.570
<i>Soon?</i>

00:14:49.550 --> 00:14:51.530
Damn, no way! Hakone Academy?

00:14:51.530 --> 00:14:53.530
No! No!

00:14:54.010 --> 00:14:57.220
Kaburagi Issa, you left 
Hakone Academy behind!

00:14:57.220 --> 00:14:59.160
Don't let them pass you!

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:03.750
What am I doing? What am I doing?

00:15:04.220 --> 00:15:05.310
<i>Damn it.</i>

00:15:05.310 --> 00:15:08.090
<i>I suddenly felt tired and 
fell behind the team.</i>

00:15:08.930 --> 00:15:13.140
<i>I only meant to rest for a second,
 but I stepped off my bike and stopped.</i>

00:15:13.140 --> 00:15:17.850
If I get left behind Hakone Academy,
 my race will be over!

00:15:17.850 --> 00:15:19.270
No!

00:15:19.270 --> 00:15:21.900
It's not over yet!

00:15:22.470 --> 00:15:24.500
<i>Crap! This isn't good!</i>

00:15:24.500 --> 00:15:25.900
<i>That's what my instincts are telling me!</i>

00:15:26.370 --> 00:15:29.330
<i>I don't have time to worry 
about Sohoku or Hakone Academy.</i>

00:15:29.750 --> 00:15:31.560
<i>Jump on the wheel in front of you.</i>

00:15:31.560 --> 00:15:33.820
<i>Then you'll make it to the front.</i>

00:15:36.230 --> 00:15:37.740
<i>I can do it!</i>

00:15:40.610 --> 00:15:42.420
The pig's wheel...

00:15:48.530 --> 00:15:50.460
I have a request, pig.

00:15:50.460 --> 00:15:53.760
Take me to the front.

00:15:54.130 --> 00:15:55.520
I'm your enemy.

00:15:55.520 --> 00:15:57.830
I know you don't like having me behind you.

00:15:57.830 --> 00:15:58.910
But...

00:15:58.910 --> 00:16:01.140
I don't want it to end yet!

00:16:01.140 --> 00:16:03.200
Let me ride here.

00:16:03.200 --> 00:16:04.150
Please, pig!

00:16:07.710 --> 00:16:09.650
That's your pride?

00:16:10.610 --> 00:16:14.280
Sticking to your opponent's behind like crap,

00:16:14.280 --> 00:16:19.250
you want an easy ride to the best part,
 so you can fight against us?

00:16:19.250 --> 00:16:22.000
Does your pride permit that?

00:16:22.000 --> 00:16:25.010
No! Of course not!

00:16:25.010 --> 00:16:27.050
But this is the only way!

00:16:27.050 --> 00:16:28.500
I don't want to do this!

00:16:28.500 --> 00:16:32.220
But my limbs are numb and won't 
move the way I want them to!

00:16:32.550 --> 00:16:34.740
I want to keep riding in the Inter-High!

00:16:34.740 --> 00:16:35.800
Please!

00:16:38.190 --> 00:16:39.870
Then don't bother.

00:16:39.870 --> 00:16:43.520
You wouldn't be able to keep up 
with Hakone Academy's pace anyway.

00:16:45.180 --> 00:16:47.130
You're a first-year, right?

00:16:47.130 --> 00:16:48.610
I'm a second-year.

00:16:48.610 --> 00:16:52.490
We'll race again next year 
in a head-to-head battle!

00:16:53.860 --> 00:16:55.570
Hey, wait!

00:16:55.570 --> 00:16:57.570
Wait, pig!

00:16:58.260 --> 00:17:00.350
Bowing your head to your enemy,

00:17:00.350 --> 00:17:04.000
abandoning your pride, and frantically 
searching for a lifeline...

00:17:04.420 --> 00:17:07.880
I don't mind guys like you.

00:17:08.230 --> 00:17:11.990
#6, Sohoku's Kaburagi Issa, has fallen.

00:17:11.990 --> 00:17:12.710
Yeah.

00:17:13.250 --> 00:17:14.740
It only took a second.

00:17:17.640 --> 00:17:19.490
Kabu...

00:17:20.550 --> 00:17:23.520
I was so focused on catching up,
 I didn't notice.

00:17:24.370 --> 00:17:25.270
How long?

00:17:25.750 --> 00:17:27.900
How long has Kaburagi been missing?

00:17:28.950 --> 00:17:31.230
Did he fall behind on the way here?

00:17:31.580 --> 00:17:33.740
<i>What are you doing, Teshima Junta?</i>

00:17:33.740 --> 00:17:36.090
M-Maybe there's something 
wrong with his bike.

00:17:36.090 --> 00:17:37.060
Like a flat tire.

00:17:37.060 --> 00:17:38.990
No, then he'd shout.

00:17:39.390 --> 00:17:41.890
We've done it countless times in practice.

00:17:41.890 --> 00:17:43.910
I told him to report any issues.

00:17:44.750 --> 00:17:46.870
M-Maybe he's not feeling well.

00:17:48.490 --> 00:17:50.790
But during this morning's meeting...

00:17:51.420 --> 00:17:53.210
It'll affect our strategy.

00:17:53.210 --> 00:17:57.170
Notify me if you don't feel well.

00:17:57.170 --> 00:17:58.930
Piece of cake.

00:17:59.350 --> 00:18:02.230
He likes to show off.

00:18:02.230 --> 00:18:05.070
He was just acting fine in front of us.

00:18:05.630 --> 00:18:09.730
He could've told me or Imaizumi-kun...

00:18:10.290 --> 00:18:15.940
Koga said lone first-years try to take on 
everything themselves at the Inter-High.

00:18:17.690 --> 00:18:18.740
<i>Koga-san...</i>

00:18:19.900 --> 00:18:25.750
Not having a classmate you can talk to 
and being a first-year on top of that

00:18:26.190 --> 00:18:28.750
puts an incredible amount of pressure on you.

00:18:29.350 --> 00:18:30.500
So much is expected of them.

00:18:30.500 --> 00:18:34.240
They're given orders, made to fight in 
an Inter-High they know nothing about,

00:18:34.240 --> 00:18:37.560
and pushed to their physical 
and mental limits.

00:18:37.560 --> 00:18:41.140
But they still desperately work 
to meet expectations.

00:18:42.230 --> 00:18:44.090
That's how it is.

00:18:44.500 --> 00:18:47.650
They're so overwhelmed,
 they don't listen to their own bodies.

00:18:48.210 --> 00:18:51.130
They only notice later,
 once they've suffered damage.

00:18:51.130 --> 00:18:52.380
Just like I did.

00:18:53.020 --> 00:18:56.870
Watch Kaburagi closely.

00:18:57.610 --> 00:18:59.690
He's a reckless idiot.

00:19:00.110 --> 00:19:02.370
He's just like I used to be.

00:19:03.100 --> 00:19:05.200
<i>When Koga-san was a first-year, he...</i>

00:19:07.870 --> 00:19:10.340
<i>After everything Koga said,</i>

00:19:10.340 --> 00:19:14.740
<i>I took my eyes off him during a moment as 
important as the start of the second day.</i>

00:19:14.740 --> 00:19:16.420
<i>What am I doing?</i>

00:19:16.420 --> 00:19:21.560
As a first-year, Kaburagi-kun was 
doing the best he could on his own.

00:19:21.560 --> 00:19:22.390
In that case...

00:19:24.060 --> 00:19:26.220
We have to go help him!

00:19:27.030 --> 00:19:28.840
Let me help him, Teshima-san!

00:19:28.840 --> 00:19:31.350
I'll drop back and bring 
him back to the team!

00:19:31.350 --> 00:19:33.230
Don't go, Onoda!

00:19:36.260 --> 00:19:38.050
Don't. You can't fall back.

00:19:38.050 --> 00:19:39.440
I won't allow you to help him.

00:19:39.800 --> 00:19:40.650
What?

00:19:40.650 --> 00:19:42.200
We'll catch up to the front.

00:19:42.200 --> 00:19:44.320
That's our top priority!

00:19:45.850 --> 00:19:49.800
We were lucky to get ahead 
of Hakone Academy. Lucky!

00:19:49.800 --> 00:19:52.830
We'll use this opportunity to 
get our team together first!

00:19:53.420 --> 00:19:57.250
If Hakone Academy gets all six members 
together first, we won't stand a chance!

00:19:57.710 --> 00:20:00.010
I'm saying I'll go alone!

00:20:00.010 --> 00:20:02.050
I promise I'll bring him back!

00:20:02.050 --> 00:20:02.890
So—

00:20:02.890 --> 00:20:03.590
No!

00:20:04.220 --> 00:20:08.530
It was the second day when you brought 
Tadokoro-san back to the team last year, too.

00:20:08.530 --> 00:20:10.340
Is that why you think you can do it?

00:20:10.340 --> 00:20:13.100
It's different now, Onoda.
 Get that through your head.

00:20:14.650 --> 00:20:18.250
You're in a different 
position from last year.

00:20:18.250 --> 00:20:21.900
You're #1, last year's champion!

00:20:21.900 --> 00:20:27.120
Not having #1 leading your 
team is like night and day!

00:20:27.630 --> 00:20:29.550
Who will stop Manami if he attacks?

00:20:29.550 --> 00:20:31.370
Who will chase after Shinkai if he attacks?

00:20:32.040 --> 00:20:34.960
Some moves can be stopped 
just by having #1 there.

00:20:35.580 --> 00:20:37.460
You have a job to do.

00:20:38.020 --> 00:20:40.800
You can't do what you want 
like you did last year.

00:20:44.780 --> 00:20:46.760
Then Kaburagi-kun...

00:20:46.760 --> 00:20:50.650
Kaburagi-kun, who worked so hard 
during the first day's sprint...

00:20:51.980 --> 00:20:53.020
We'll leave him behind.

00:20:55.140 --> 00:20:56.870
Let's at least wait!

00:20:56.870 --> 00:20:59.690
We can drop our pace,
 so Kaburagi-kun can catch up!

00:20:59.690 --> 00:21:00.320
We can't.

00:21:00.320 --> 00:21:00.940
We can!

00:21:00.940 --> 00:21:04.220
No. We can't, Onoda.

00:21:04.950 --> 00:21:08.950
Look. Hakone Academy's right behind us!

00:21:12.370 --> 00:21:14.590
<i>Sorry, Kaburagi.</i>

00:21:14.590 --> 00:21:17.960
<i>You worked so hard on the 
first day as a first-year.</i>

00:21:19.210 --> 00:21:20.770
We'll catch up to the rest of the team!

00:21:20.770 --> 00:21:22.510
Eyes forward, everyone!

00:21:23.390 --> 00:21:27.130
<i>Hakone Academy passed Kaburagi-kun.</i>

00:21:27.130 --> 00:21:29.490
<i>He must be in pretty bad shape.</i>

00:21:29.490 --> 00:21:31.140
<i>I need to go help him.</i>

00:21:31.140 --> 00:21:32.310
<i>But I can't.</i>

00:21:32.310 --> 00:21:34.230
Face forward!

00:21:34.230 --> 00:21:35.440
Yes, sir.

00:21:35.890 --> 00:21:38.770
Junta, I just remembered 
I have something to do.

00:21:40.310 --> 00:21:41.820
Can I drop back?

00:21:45.010 --> 00:21:48.430
I forgot an idiot behind us.

00:23:26.840 --> 00:23:28.010
Shut up!

00:23:36.370 --> 00:23:40.020
<i>NEXT LINE  Sash of Wishes</i>

00:23:40.020 --> 00:23:45.020
